# Saving and loading a game against the computer. The harness keeps saves in memory; tests/ui/records holds two vs-Computer records
# (a comment line `# vs-computer: you=... level=... seed=...`, see docs/NOTATION.md).
# Layout (1400x800): main menu without a save: Versus (150,250), Load game (150,310); with an autosave: Continue (150,220), Versus (150,280).
#   Load screen slot rows (600,166+64*i); in game Back (125,25), Submit (841,90), Undo (558,90).
wait 20
slot 1 ../records/vs-white-easy.5dr      # the computer's reply to e4 is already in it: White to move
slot 2 ../records/vs-black-easy.5dr      # Black to move, White's opening is the computer's
click 150 310        # Load game
wait 40
capture vs-load-screen               # "Standard vs Computer - 2 turns" and "... - 1 turn"
click 600 230        # slot 2: playing Black
wait 120
capture vs-load-black                # loaded as vs-Computer: Black to move, the player's turn, Undo disabled
clicksq 0 1 c7
wait 40
clicksq 0 1 c5
wait 40
click 841 90         # Submit; the computer answers as White, and the autosave notes the mode
waitai
wait 90
capture vs-load-black-replied
click 125 25         # Back to the mode list
wait 30
click 700 712        # Back to the main menu
wait 40
click 150 220        # Continue
wait 120
capture vs-continue-resumed          # the same game with its three turns, Black to move
click 558 90         # Undo: the player's turn and the computer's reply: back to the opening
wait 60
capture vs-continue-undo
